# Google Wallet / Firebase service account credentials
crp-tester-card-*.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
serviceAccount*.json
# The Worker key normally lives outside the repo (~/), but ignore it here too
# in case it is ever copied in — a committed key cannot be un-leaked.
crp-worker-key*.json
*-worker-key*.json
private_key*.json

# NOTE: js/firebase-config.js and admin/js/firebase-config.js are intentionally
# COMMITTED. They are Firebase *web* configs, which are public identifiers by
# design and grant no data access on their own — firestore.rules is the
# protection. This repo is a static site served straight to visitors, so the
# config has to be present in the deployment. Never gitignore service account
# keys or Admin SDK credentials; those are the real secrets.

# Firebase
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firebase-debug.*.log
firestore-debug.log
ui-debug.log
*-debug.log
database-debug.log
.firebaserc.bak

# Node
node_modules/
functions/node_modules/

# Emulator / test artifacts
firestore-debug.log
coverage/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.*
# ...but the example template must stay committed, or there is nothing to
# copy from. This negation has to come after the patterns above to win.
!.env.example
!**/.env.example